   $q$A bag holds 6 green marbles and some blue marbles. The probability of drawing a green marble at random is $\frac{2}{5}$. How many blue marbles are in the bag?$q$, $q$[{"text":"6","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-equal-numbers-of-each-color"},{"text":"3","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-the-fraction-numbers-without-scaling"},{"text":"15","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-the-total-number-of-marbles"},{"text":"9","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$9$q$, $q$Green is $\frac{2}{5}$ of the marbles, so $6$ is $\frac{2}{5}$ of the total. Each fifth is $6 \div 2 = 3$ marbles, so the total is $5 \times 3 = 15$. The blue marbles are $15 - 6 = 9$. The value 15 is the total, not the number of blue marbles.$q$, 'draft', null)
